    "minimumForDiagnosis": "Protein-losing enteropathy demonstrated by low albumin/protein plus elevated fecal alpha-1-antitrypsin, combined with histological evidence of dilated intestinal lymphatics.",
    "notes": "Primary form (Waldmann disease) is congenital. Secondary forms result from conditions causing lymphatic obstruction (constrictive pericarditis, lymphoma, Fontan procedure, SLE, sarcoidosis)."
  },
